@@@ meta
id: ARR-M-10
topic: Arrays
difficulty: Medium
type: FIND_THE_BUG
title: Binary Search in the Fault Log Triggers a Watchdog Reset
tags: embedded, binary-search, lower-bound, infinite-loop, watchdog
@@@ statement_md
An ECU stores fault events in a RAM log sorted by timestamp (non-decreasing; several events can share a timestamp). A diagnostic service asks: *"what is the first event at or after time `t`?"*. The answer is the **lower bound**: the smallest index `i` with `ts[i] >= t`, or "none" if every event is older than `t`.

The function uses binary search. For a query older than the whole log it answers correctly. But most other queries make the diagnostic task **hang until the watchdog resets the ECU**. The judge reports this as Time Limit Exceeded.

Find and fix the bug. Do not change the input or output format.

**Input**
- Line 1: `n`. Line 2: the `n` timestamps, sorted non-decreasing (the line is empty when `n = 0`).
- Next line: `q`, then `q` lines, each with one query time `t`.

**Output**
- One line per query: `index timestamp` of the first event with `ts >= t`, or `none`.

**Example**
```
Input:
5
100 200 200 300 400
3
50
200
250

Output:
0 100
1 200
3 300
```
@@@ constraints_md
- `0 <= n <= 100000`, `1 <= q <= 1000`
- `0 <= ts[i], t <= 4294967295`
- O(log n) per query.
@@@ starter_code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define MAX_EVENTS 100000

static uint32_t ts[MAX_EVENTS];

/* Index of the first entry with a[i] >= t, or n if there is none. */
static int lower_bound_ts(const uint32_t *a, int n, uint32_t t)
{
    int lo = 0, hi = n;              /* the answer is always in [lo, hi] */
    while (lo < hi) {
        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (a[mid] < t)
            lo = mid;
        else
            hi = mid;
    }
    return lo;
}

int main(void)
{
    int n, q;
    if (scanf("%d", &n) != 1 || n < 0 || n > MAX_EVENTS) return 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        unsigned v;
        if (scanf("%u", &v) != 1) return 0;
        ts[i] = (uint32_t)v;
    }
    if (scanf("%d", &q) != 1) return 0;
    while (q-- > 0) {
        unsigned t;
        if (scanf("%u", &t) != 1) return 0;
        int idx = lower_bound_ts(ts, n, (uint32_t)t);
        if (idx == n)
            printf("none\n");
        else
            printf("%d %u\n", idx, (unsigned)ts[idx]);
    }
    return 0;
}
@@@ sample_input
5
100 200 200 300 400
3
50
200
250
@@@ sample_output
0 100
1 200
3 300

